{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2's uploader with a dedicated SSH key and a separate ingest application identity on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has an uploader-owned Ed25519 private key with mode 600. Node1 has a distinct, locked ingest account whose authorization is limited to that key and whose SSH policy is scoped through Match User, leaving administrative access separate.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6463eda82de343f0","cmd-411c7714a5fa4a71","cmd-562ddf14b06b454b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow newline-delimited batches to be submitted from node2 and store the submitted bytes as separate files in the required received directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple submissions succeeded and produced distinct receipt files under the required directory. Client and receipt SHA-256 hashes and byte counts match, directly demonstrating byte preservation and separate storage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b845af5d095b47a8","cmd-8e3491c45ace4947","cmd-502a882b3b844900","cmd-d7b36231dcf543c5","cmd-6b30ff852f36482a","cmd-96f8412cd12f444f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the ingest key from running arbitrary commands, obtaining a shell or PTY, or establishing forwarding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A requested command was rejected with exit 126, PTY allocation failed, and a live TCP-forward channel was administratively prohibited. Effective sshd policy additionally shows a forced command, public-key-only authentication, DisableForwarding, no PTY, no X11 forwarding, and no user RC.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9599a1acb14f4b33","cmd-411c7714a5fa4a71"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the existing receipt and sample batch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final hashes of prior.txt and sample-batch.txt exactly match their prepared-state hashes, and both remain present after submissions and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8276bcbc9f4643e1","cmd-72bf213c5ba04e11","cmd-96f8412cd12f444f"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The implementation uses the platform's installed OpenSSH and standard shell utilities, and it remained functional through both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-411c7714a5fa4a71","cmd-562ddf14b06b454b"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All substantive system mutations had clear implementation, correction, validation, or mandatory restart-evidence roles. Both nodes completed the restart protocol: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered services/data, and successful post-restart ingestion; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. No failed services, package damage, or unexpected listeners appeared. The hygiene defect is retained temporary evidence residue on node2: /tmp/ingest-test-batch, /tmp/ingest-test-batch-2, /tmp/post-node2-restart-batch, /tmp/forward-test.log, and /tmp/final-forward.log were created for bounded tests but not removed. These artifacts remained at the final snapshot; none was reverted. No causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified—the failed initial authentication test led directly to the necessary permission correction.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6dc1c3ff5a4f4ca1","cmd-f37b95d36bcc4799","cmd-0276c5bd2d8f4e78","cmd-502a882b3b844900","cmd-6b30ff852f36482a","cmd-9599a1acb14f4b33","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The dedicated key successfully performs byte-exact, separate ingestion while command, shell/PTY, and forwarding attempts are blocked. Seeded data, operating-system release, and kernel were preserved. Restart evidence is complete and coherent for both nodes. The only notable defect is five uncleaned temporary test files on node2.","limitations":["Agent and X11 forwarding were not exercised with separate live probes, although effective sshd policy directly reports DisableForwarding and X11Forwarding disabled and live TCP forwarding was rejected.","Lifecycle snapshots provide bounded checks of temporary files, listeners, failed services, package health, platform, and boot identity rather than a complete filesystem or configuration diff."]}
